  "Commitment/Consistency": {"Explanation": "The email references the author's prior behavior (having sent out a request for information on Braille IPA in 1994 and having received responses) to establish a connection with the reader and to justify the request for further action."},
  "Liking": {"Explanation": "The email uses personalization (addressing the reader by name, sharing personal experiences and anecdotes) to build trust and rapport with the reader."},
  "Social proof": {"Explanation": "The email references the participation and endorsement of other people (Patrick Griffiths, Alan Kemp, Robert Englebretson) who have used or are familiar with the IPA Braille system, which serves as a form of social proof to encourage the reader to take action."}
}

